Common Commands for a Hyphen File
• View its contents: cat ./-
• Check its file type: file ./-
• See its details/permissions: ls -l ./-
• Delete the file: rm ./-

OPEN FILE: starts with dashes and it contains spaces.

VIEW:-
Path Prefix + Quotes (Recommended): cat "./--spaces in this filename--" 
---(The ./ stops the terminal from seeing the starting dashes as options, and the quotes handle the spaces)
Double Dash + Quotes: cat "./--spaces in this filename--"
---(• The -- tells the command to stop looking for options, and the quotes handle the spaces).

EDIT

nano "./--spaces in this filename--"
vim "./--spaces in this filename--"

TIP: Type cat ./--s and press the Tab key.
